  "findings": [
    "The exact pre-change native baseline admits a nonowner shared Child comment and duplicates clock-derived comment/history IDs; both retained AssertionErrors now have direct regressions.",
    "Actual HTTP mention failure exposed sender-bound recipient lookup. The internal adapter reads the live recipient identity separately while the caller remains the owning comment I01 command.",
    "Actual SSE failure exposed previous-audience union with global notification invalidation. New mentions use server-owned recipient scope; wire events contain no titles, content or IDs.",
    "First full suite8500pass/2fail retained: explicit legacy transaction ownership join added without a static allowlist, and the intentional P12 comment policy transition retains all old assertions while adding negative read-scope checks.",
    "Comments, history and mentions share the canonical Task payload/revision and I01 receipt. No duplicate comment database, scheduler, provider call or public API.",
    "Opaque session-owned uncertain comment and grant packets survive native SSE/navigation with unchanged body/revision/key, but fresh Task or manager-scope loss/logout retires them and fences late effects.",
    "Three browser journeys cover Unicode comment/mention lost ACK through Calendar navigation, reviewed list grant lost ACK through drawer navigation, and real SSE revocation of private history/composer; all four parent Calendar journeys also pass."
  ],
